# Global Standards

Any task begins with the pipeline in `agent-pipeline.mdc`; domain standards live in their own rules and the pipeline enforces them.

## Rule routing

Glob-scoped rules (`alwaysApply: false`) are not always auto-attached, so before planning or editing in an area, read the matching rule:

- React / UI / screens / components → `react-patterns`, `engineering-standards`, `constants`
- New or changed behaviour, tests, mocks, Zustand stores → `test-driven-development`
- New `src/` folders or rewired imports → `fsd-layers` (boundaries are CI law)
- Data fetching, async, error handling, logging, stores → `resilience`, `engineering-standards`
- `app.config.ts`, `babel.config.js`, `metro.config.js`, `package.json`, `tsconfig.json` → `project-config`

## Always

- **English** for code, comments, commits and repo docs. Prefer existing libraries over custom infrastructure; minimalist code.
- **Authority**: `AGENTS.md` § Source of truth (code is ground truth, `AGENTS.md` the canonical guide, `.cursor/brain/` the depth layer); sync drift in the same session.
- User-visible copy lives in `src/shared/locales/**`; logic and public UI APIs use constants, tokens or typed keys instead of unexplained literals.
